{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Day With Vanessa"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Walking and Talking"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About the Future - If, When, Before and After"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use time clauses to give information about time and sequence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words If, When, Before and After in time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the first conditional with these time clauses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:<br/>If/When/Before/After + Subject + Simple Present tense, Subject + will + Simple Present tense"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Before</span> means at an earlier time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">After</span> means at a later time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Before I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm.<br/>After I set my alarm, I'll go to sleep.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If</span> means on the condition that ..."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If I go to sleep, I'll set my alarm.</span> (I'm not sure that I'll go to sleep)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When</span> means at the time of doing something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">When I go to bed, I'll set my alarm.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When I see one at the store, I'll call you! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "After I get home tonight, I'll try and get creative. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before I go in tomorrow, I'll send you a list of ideas to write about. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you send me a text to remind me, I won't forget! "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing You Understand Someone's Feelings or Emotions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In conversation, it is natural to show that you understand someone's feelings and emotions. It helps to use different kinds of structures and expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structures:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You<span class=\"strong\"> ought to be/ must be</span> +adjective<br/>It <span class=\"strong\">ought to be</span>/must be + adjective<br/>You've /It's <span class=\"strong\">got to be</span> +adjective<br/>I'm sure that's/you're + adjective<br/>Aren't you + adjective?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use these expressions:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I get it.<br/>I know what you mean.<br/>I hear you.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must be freezing in that tank top, Sally!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You've got to be boiling in that duffel coat. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Aren't you tired of inventing new dishes every week?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "duffel coat"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a warm coat made of duffel (a kind of wool)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You've got to be boiling in that duffel coat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs and work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "material"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "facts, information or ideas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm running out of material to blog about."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to invent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to create something new"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Aren't you tired of inventing new dishes every week?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to manage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be in charge of; to su